<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yahya ibn Ghaniya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1237</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Yahya ibn Ishaq ibn Ghaniya</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yahya ibn Ghaniya was a leader of the Banu Ghaniya, heirs of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a>, who continued his brother Ali's war against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad Caliphate</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a> for about half a century. Allied with Arab tribes, he took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdia">Mahdia</a> around 1203 and killed his former ally Qaraqush around 1212. His long campaigns ravaged the towns and countryside of Ifriqiya and Tripolitania before his death in the 1230s.</p></div>
